WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:04.529
The final episode of The Expanse is out now.

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:11.030
Amos rides a rocket through a sci-fi kaleidoscope,
Marco is eaten by interdimensional aliens,

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.219
and Drummer becomes queen of space.

00:00:14.219 --> 00:00:15.379
What does it all mean?

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:17.740
What are the hidden easter eggs and references?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.119
And how does the final season compare to the
books?

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:24.699
Season 6 is based on the sixth Expanse book,
Babylon’s Ashes.

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:30.039
But it also includes the story from an Expanse
novella, called Strange Dogs.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:36.120
So the episode starts on Laconia – the planet
ruled by Duarte, who led a bunch of rogue

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:42.379
Martians here last season . Duarte and the
scientist Cortazar experiment with the protomolecule,

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:47.449
trying to control these mysterious structures
orbiting the planet.

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:53.219
This girl Cara is the daughter of some scientists
on Laconia, and she has encountered some strange

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.660
alien dogs.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.750
The dogs fix Cara’s broken drone.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:03.219
They fix a dead bird, bringing it back to
life as a creepy zombie bird.

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:07.100
And now they fix Cara’s dead brother, Xan.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.189
Cause these dogs aren’t ordinary natural
animals.

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:16.560
They are “repair drones” – technological
“constructs” , created by the alien builders

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.250
billions of years ago to automatically fix
things.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:28.540
Their faces are described as looking embarrassed
in the books , and they like to say “ki-ka-ko”

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:35.090
. The aliens that created the dogs are long
extinct now, but the dogs still keep trying

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:40.930
to fix things – even though they don’t
really understand how a human is supposed

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:41.930
to work.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.580
So after they fix Xan, Xan is different.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:51.430
He says he feels weird , and he sees things
he couldn’t see before in glowing blue CGI

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:57.320
. It’s like what happened to Katoa in Season
3, when he was changed by the protomolecule

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:03.680
. The dogs haven’t just fixed Xan, they’ve
upgraded him with alien biotech.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.480
So is Xan still fully human, or is he something
else now?

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.160
Cara is just happy that she gets her brother
back.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.620
But when she brings him home, her parents
Gary and Dot are horrified.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.670
They reject their zombie son, and attack him,
to Cara’s horror.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:26.780
Because Cara and her parents have different
worldviews – they literally grew up on different

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.910
worlds.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.640
Gary and Dot are from on Earth, where death
is permanent.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:37.780
But Cara grew up on Laconia, where death can
be fixed by the dogs – that’s normal to

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.780
her, cause it’s all she knows.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:44.180
Like many real immigrant families, Cara’s
parents have different rules and expectations

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:49.690
about the world than she does , and tragically,
this tears their family apart.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:54.620
So Cara tricks her parents with a recording
of her voice and runs into the forest with

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.620
Xan.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.660
She knows she’ll die out here, without food
or water – but says the strange dogs will

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:06.550
fix her if she dies . That’s the end of
the story for Cara and Lil Xan in the TV show

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:10.200
– but their story continues in the Expanse
books.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.760
The Expanse TV show only adapts the first
six books, though there are three more books

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.000
beyond that.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.640
Hopefully the rest of the story will be adapted
one day.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:25.790
Back in the Sol system, Earth, Mars and Drummer’s
Belters plan their attack against Marco.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.700
For most of the series, Earth and Mars were
enemies, and the Belt was exploited by the

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.200
inner planets.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.700
These years of oppression and war have not
been forgotten – it wasn’t that long ago

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:43.550
Avasarala was hanging Belters on hooks . But
Earth Mars and Belt are now forced to work

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.580
together against the greater threat of Marco.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:52.010
Cause if Marco’s navy gets to Medina Station
in the ring space, defended by Laconian rail

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:58.691
guns, Marco could solidify control over all
the ring gates – dictator of a thousand

00:03:58.691 --> 00:04:05.040
worlds . Since Duarte gave Marco a bunch of
Mars’ ships, and Earth’s fleet was degraded

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:11.480
by years of pointless war , their combined
forces might not be enough to stop Marco . So

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.650
Plan B is for the Roci crew and a ship called
the Giambattista to race for the ring space

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:23.090
and capture Marco’s rail guns before he
gets there . It’s a wildly dangerous, desperate

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:28.640
mission, so of course Holden is very optimistic
that it’ll go great .

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:34.110
Bobbie and Holden take a moment to remember
Alex, who died last season.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:39.050
Alex was kinda the social glue that held the
Roci crew together.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:45.130
His friendly easy-going personality balanced
out the extreme personalities of Holden Naomi

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.460
and Amos.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:51.100
While the rest of the crew battled aliens
and saved the universe, he often stayed on

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:57.360
the ship and looked after their home, he made
sure everyone was eating and cared for, he

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.320
was like a parent.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.310
So when Alex died, and Clarissa and Bobbie
joined the crew, the whole dynamic of their

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:11.360
family was disrupted, and the crew almost
broke apart . Amos almost quit after Holden

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:17.060
spared Filip . Holden was uncomfortable with
Clarissa, who did try to kill him a few times.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:21.040
And Naomi didn’t like Amos and Clarissa’s
friendship.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:26.290
Cause it used to be Amos and Naomi who had
a special close relationship.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:33.350
In Season 1, they were both damaged, vulnerable
people, so they supported each other – Amos

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:39.130
protected Naomi, and Naomi guided Amos, he
called her his “boss”.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.170
But now, Amos has.. grown up, become a leader
himself.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:49.060
Now, he guides Clarissa, and she calls him
boss.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:54.830
So now, Naomi understands and accepts this
relationship , and welcomes Clarissa as a

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.639
member of their family.

00:05:56.639 --> 00:05:59.060
But Clarissa is dying.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:04.610
Cause back in Season 3, she tried to kill
Holden as revenge for the downfall of her

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:05.900
father, Jules-Pierre.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:11.200
Clarissa got illegal biotech mods implanted
into her body that can enhance her strength

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.980
and speed for short bursts.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:17.000
But these mods are.. not FDA approved.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.760
They constantly leech hormones into her body,
damaging her health.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:27.990
And now she learns she’s only got about
five years to live . The screen says that

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:31.610
“salt craving” is one of the symptoms
of her condition – which explains why she

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:38.420
ate so much salt in Episode 4 . Clarissa knows
her time is running out, and she chooses to

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:43.830
spend her last years with her new family,
cooking a proper meal for them all, like Alex

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.210
used to do.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:52.210
In Book 6, Naomi thinks she treasures her
time with her loved ones, because it won’t

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:53.600
last forever.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:58.340
Everything ends, and that’s what makes these
moments precious .

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:03.960
Drummer prepares for battle with Marco – the
man who killed her friend Ashford, killed

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.770
her friend Fred, and killed her partner Serge.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:12.220
The man who started the war that broke her
family apart.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:17.500
She flies Ashford’s ship the Tynan into
battle, and she’s convinced a Belter leader

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.460
called Walker to join her side.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.700
In the book, there’s a whole plotline about
Holden trying to convince a diverse bunch

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:31.450
of Belter OPA leaders to work with Earth and
Mars against Marco . Fred Johnson was the

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:36.960
best hope to unite the OPA in cooperation
with the inners, but Fred suddenly dies in

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:42.010
Book 6 . So it’s only with the help of Dawes
that Holden’s able to bring the Belters

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:46.380
together .
Drummer and her allies attack Marco, but Marco

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:52.130
pulls a sneaky trick by disguising his ship
the Pella as a different ship.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:57.750
Kinda like how the Roci was once disguised
as a harmless gas freighter . Marco counterattacks

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:02.830
and cripples Drummer’s ship – ending her
chance for revenge.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:07.780
Drummer had to swallow her pride join Earth
and Mars against Marco.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:14.100
She left her family behind to fight this war,
and now she just suffers more defeat.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:21.010
She feels she’s lost everything, that this
universe has no place for her . So in rage

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:26.880
and despair, she tries a suicide attack on
Marco , but Walker beats her to it.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:31.040
Is there a place for Drummer in this universe?

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:35.830
In the book, Drummer’s plotline is taken
by a similar character called Michio Pa.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:41.110
In her battle with Marco, Pa is badly burned,
and forced to recover in a makeshift hospital

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:49.279
in a luxury resort on Titan . It’s a strange,
surreal scene, in limbo between life and death,

00:08:49.279 --> 00:08:50.279
inner planets and Belt.

00:08:50.279 --> 00:08:57.080
Pa grapples with all she’s lost, before
rising reborn and finding new purpose.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:02.360
So while Drummer, Earth and Mars distract
Marco, the Roci and the Giambattista get to

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:03.650
the ring space.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:08.790
Bobbie and Amos are in the assault team attacking
the ring station to take the rail guns.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:12.860
We see this list of the other soldiers on
the assault team, and most of these names

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.580
are references to famous sci fi stories.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:20.020
Ripley, Vasquez, Hicks and Hudson are characters
from the Alien movies.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:24.710
The creators of The Expanse have said that
Alien was a huge influence on the series,

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:30.130
specifically in how it portrayed average people
with blue-collar jobs in space – like the

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.760
crew of the Cant in Season 1.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:32.760
Vasquez Hicks and Hudson are from the second
Alien movie, where they land on mysterious

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:33.760
alien territory for a dangerous mission – just
like what they’re doing now in The Expanse.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:38.340
We also see the names of Admiral Ackbar from
Star Wars, David Bowman from 2001 , Commander

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:43.529
Shepherd from Mass Effect, Duncan Idaho from
Dune, Rick Deckard from Blade Runner, Jack

00:09:43.529 --> 00:09:49.090
O’Neill from Stargate, Johnny Rico from
Starship Troopers, Sarah Connor from Terminator,

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:51.240
and Will Riker from Star Trek.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:56.970
So these are some of the greatest badasses
in sci fi history – and Bobbie Draper and

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.520
Amos Burton are right there with them.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:04.350
There are more easter eggs in these names
– comment below if you spot one.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:10.290
The Giambattista dumps lots of empty containers
as decoys, to provide cover for the assault

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:12.950
team as they drop onto the ring station.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:18.230
One of the containers has the logo of Mao-Kwikowski
Mercantile – that was the company of Jules-Pierre

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:22.520
Mao before he was imprisoned for his protomolecule
conspiracy.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.600
The “Mao” part of the logo has been scrubbed
off.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:31.660
Jules-Pierre’s daughter, Clarissa, struggles
with her father’s legacy, as we see in a

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.790
bonus scene for this season.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:38.810
There are five bonus scenes in Season 6, and
you can watch them on Amazon Prime Video,

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:44.860
on a phone, PC, or Fire TV , by clicking X-Ray
in the top left, then Bonus Content.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:50.050
The Episode 4 bonus scene follows Clarissa,
as she finds out that her father Jules-Pierre

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:52.080
has died in jail.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:58.180
She hates that she always wanted the approval
of such a terrible dad . So much of the evil

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:02.060
she did in Season 3 was to try and win his
love.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:06.790
But now she’s found a better family with
Amos and the Roci crew.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:11.529
At the end of the scene, Clarissa starts to
clean up a mess she made – she likes fixing

00:11:11.529 --> 00:11:17.250
things now, cause that represents making up
for her mistakes . And she continues that

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:22.399
in the finale – heroically risking her life
to repair the Roci mid-battle.

00:11:22.399 --> 00:11:25.850
Meanwhile, the assault team land on the ring
station.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:32.290
Amos survives a sci-fi high-g clusterfuck,
while Bobbie makes a more dignified entrance.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:36.980
But the assault goes badly, and many of the
team are killed – RIP Hudson.

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.810
“Game over man, game over!”.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:45.090
In the book, the soldiers defending the ring
station are Duarte’s rogue Martians, helping

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:46.180
Marco.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:51.710
So Bobbie loves the opportunity to get revenge
against the Martian traitors who betrayed

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:57.860
her homeworld . Bobbie goes all Iron Man and
defeats the enemy, but is forced to destroy

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.590
the rail guns with a missile.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:05.600
Which was not the plan – they hoped to capture
the rail guns, so they could use them against

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.060
Marco when he arrives.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.570
But Bobbie had no other choice.

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:12.440
In the book, it’s different.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.660
Bobbie tries to capture the rail guns by just
blowing up their power source.

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:21.330
But the explosion causes a reaction from the
ring station itself.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:28.200
The entire station turns green and it physically
expands, breaking the rail guns – like how

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.149
it reacted to an explosion in Season 3.

00:12:31.149 --> 00:12:36.790
Bobbie’s attack seems to make the station
angry . So this is a reminder that the ring

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:43.040
space is a remnant of a vast and mysterious
alien empire, and humanity is messing with

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.959
powerful forces that they do not understand.

00:12:45.959 --> 00:12:52.220
But point is, the rail guns are broken, leaving
the Roci is alone and defenceless , with all

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:57.700
the power of Marco’s Free Navy burning hard
to destroy them.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:01.820
On the way to the ring, Marco gets a message
from Duarte on Laconia.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:07.589
Duarte is an important ally for Marco – Duarte
gave him his ships and his rail guns.

00:13:07.589 --> 00:13:13.120
And Marco hinted earlier that he’s expecting
more from Duarte soon , like some secret weapon

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.430
or reinforcements or something.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:20.450
But now Duarte tells Marco to get fucked,
he’s on his own – Laconia won’t help

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:25.300
Marco any more . Cause all along, Duarte was
using Marco.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:30.050
He only gave Marco ships and weapons so that
he’d keep Earth and Mars busy so Duarte

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:36.060
could settle on Laconia undisturbed . Having
Marco in the ring space was a useful buffer,

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:41.350
so that to get to Laconia, people would have
to get through Marco first . Duarte’s tone

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:46.839
is kinda mean and vindictive here – he enjoys
disrespecting Marco.

00:13:46.839 --> 00:13:51.920
But in the book, Duarte is more respectful
and sincere.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:57.180
Duarte really believes he’s doing what’s
best for humanity – and that’s part of

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.270
what makes him so dangerous.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:04.820
Duarte says he has “have gods to kill”
. Because Duarte’s mission is to defeat

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.550
the mysterious entities in the ring gates.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:13.890
Duarte is building a great Laconian empire
empowered by alien technology to save humanity

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:16.850
from this interdimensional threat.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:23.090
So Duarte and Laconia have a really cool plotline,
which continues in the next three Expanse

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.140
books.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:28.090
Duarte’s rejection is a huge loss to Marco.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:33.670
But when Filip turns up, Marco hides his rage
and acts like everything’s going great.

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:38.010
Marco constantly lies and bullshits everyone
around him.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:43.570
He said himself that he tells people whatever
they need to hear . The books emphasise how

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:49.769
whenever he fails at something, he acts like
that was actually his plan all along . Marco

00:14:49.769 --> 00:14:53.880
manipulates everyone – including his son.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:57.480
This season, Filip questions his loyalty to
Marco.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:02.870
Filip feels guilt for helping Marco kill billions
of people on Earth, and guilt for killing

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:06.690
his friend Yoan out of stupid misdirected
rage.

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:11.730
He meets this guy Tadeo, and learns that Tadeo
had a brother who was killed by Marco’s

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:13.850
bombs on Ceres.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:19.730
Last season, Naomi told Filip that Marco made
him a murderer, and one day Filip will feel

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:24.080
guilt for his crimes . And now that day has
come.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:29.140
Filip is shaken by the death of Rosenfeld,
and tells Marco it could have been Filip who

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:35.450
died . But Marco doesn’t care, and says
he’d be proud if Filip died for his cause

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:40.680
. Last season, Naomi told Filip that Marco
would let Filip die for him, but Marco wouldn’t

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:44.810
die for Filip . Now Filip sees she was right.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:45.810
Marco only really loves himself.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:49.140
Marco gives a big speech about how his revolution
will free the Belter people.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.589
But now Filip sees that’s not true.

00:15:52.589 --> 00:15:56.260
Marco abandoned millions of Belters to die
on Ceres.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:00.000
Marco doesn’t listen to Sanjrani’s plans
to feed the Belt.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.110
He’s more interested in his personal vendettas
against Drummer, Holden and Naomi.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:09.360
Marco’s revolution only serves himself.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:15.079
Filip finally sees that his father is nothing
more than a selfish manipulative murderer

00:16:15.079 --> 00:16:18.959
.
Last season, Naomi told Filip that sometimes,

00:16:18.959 --> 00:16:24.940
the only choice is to walk away . And so now,
Filip walks away.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:30.329
He leaves Marco on his own ship, and escapes
his controlling father.

00:16:30.329 --> 00:16:36.670
He rejects the Inaros name, and instead names
himself Filip Nagata, after his mother.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:40.100
Naomi never finds out that Filip escaped Marco.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.100
She thinks that she failed to save him last
season.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.839
But her words free her son.

00:16:43.839 --> 00:16:49.839
The Roci crew stand alone in the ring space
– apparently Sarah Connor and Duncan Idaho

00:16:49.839 --> 00:16:50.890
didn’t make it.

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:56.580
They’re outnumbered and outgunned by Marco’s
Free Navy, so they prepare for a heroic last

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.600
stand.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:03.050
But then Naomi suggests that they wake the
mysterious alien entities.

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:07.369
These entities have been destroying ships
that go through the ring – like the Barkeith

00:17:07.369 --> 00:17:08.720
last season.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:13.419
Naomi and the scientist Elvi figured out that
these entities become active after a certain

00:17:13.419 --> 00:17:18.769
amount of mass and energy goes through the
ring . So just as Marco arrives, the Roci

00:17:18.769 --> 00:17:23.970
crew throw the Giambattista through a ring
to activate the entities, and so Marco is

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:27.319
obliterated along with his navy, right at
the moment he thought he was victorious.

00:17:27.319 --> 00:17:32.400
It’s kinda like Gollum dying amidst orange
CGI at his moment of victory in Lord of the

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.400
Rings.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.139
There’s even a ring.

00:17:35.139 --> 00:17:40.139
In the books, when the entities kill people,
people experience changes to their perception

00:17:40.139 --> 00:17:41.659
and consciousness.

00:17:41.659 --> 00:17:47.299
In Marco’s last moments he stops seeing
objects, and instead sees the molecules those

00:17:47.299 --> 00:17:51.429
objects are made of, and the photons bouncing
off them.

00:17:51.429 --> 00:17:55.169
Instead of hearing sound he perceives the
vibrations in the air.

00:17:55.169 --> 00:18:01.869
His sense of self melts into a cloud of energy
– before the entities slither through the

00:18:01.869 --> 00:18:08.190
nothingness and sweep him to oblivion . The
entities manipulate consciousness itself as

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:13.780
a weapon, and these ideas are explored more
in the last few Expanse books.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:18.629
So the Roci crew kill Marco and finally end
this terrible war.

00:18:18.629 --> 00:18:23.799
The horror for Naomi is that she believes
she has killed her son Filip.

00:18:23.799 --> 00:18:29.030
Never knowing that Filip actually left Marco
and survived, inspired by her words.

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:33.409
Later, Naomi says that all we can do is try
to help others.

00:18:33.409 --> 00:18:38.289
It doesn’t matter if we ever know we made
a difference, it’s not about making ourselves

00:18:38.289 --> 00:18:39.379
feel good.

00:18:39.379 --> 00:18:45.269
But the right kind word might change someone’s
life, so it’s always worth trying .

00:18:45.269 --> 00:18:51.440
There’s a big meeting with the leaders of
Earth Mars and the Belt, to figure out “the

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:58.029
architecture by which we try to unfuck ourselves”,
as Avasarala says in the books . She says

00:18:58.029 --> 00:19:04.139
war doesn’t end on the battlefield – war
ends at the negotiating table . Cause killing

00:19:04.139 --> 00:19:06.169
Marco was the easy part.

00:19:06.169 --> 00:19:09.899
The hard part is making a peace that will
last.

00:19:09.899 --> 00:19:14.860
Unless they can build more fair and stable
political order , they’ll just end up with

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:23.149
more war in the future – as Drummer said,
Marco’s extremism was inevitable in an unjust

00:19:23.149 --> 00:19:25.190
unequal system.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:30.409
The big problem, especially in the book, is
that the Belt doesn’t have a future.

00:19:30.409 --> 00:19:35.470
The whole reason why Belters exist was originally
to mine resources in the asteroid belt.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:40.659
Over the generations, their culture and bodies
adapted to life in low gravity.

00:19:40.659 --> 00:19:45.059
But now, through the ring gates, there are
thousands of new habitable planets, with free

00:19:45.059 --> 00:19:51.070
air and water, where it’s way easier to
get resources . These new worlds are the future

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:52.149
of humanity.

00:19:52.149 --> 00:19:58.160
But Belters have no place in this future . Because
most Belters, like Naomi, can’t survive

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:02.399
on planets with gravity, because their bodies
are adapted to space.

00:20:02.399 --> 00:20:06.859
And those Belters who can live on planets,
within a few generations, won’t really be

00:20:06.859 --> 00:20:14.100
Belters any more . The Belter, as a people
and a culture, face extinction . Marco’s

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:18.499
solution to this problem was to block off
the ring gates, so Earth and Mars would still

00:20:18.499 --> 00:20:24.809
need the Belt . He wanted to preserve the
status quo, just with Belters in charge instead

00:20:24.809 --> 00:20:31.070
of the inners . But now the leaders of Earth
Mars and Belt find a better solution, looking

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:34.120
to the future instead of the past.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:39.200
They form a Transport Union to govern the
shipping and trade between the ring gates.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:44.470
It’s really important to have someone coordinating
ring transits , because otherwise people might

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:50.100
accidentally get eaten by the entities . And
there needs to be a lot of trade right now,

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:55.200
because since Marco broke Earth, and was blocking
off the ring gates, the colony worlds and

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:58.780
damaged Earth are desperate for each other’s
resources.

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:03.029
Plus many people want to leave Earth and Mars
to settle on the colony worlds.

00:21:03.029 --> 00:21:09.320
So there’s a lot of work to be done coordinating
transport and trade in space, and Belters

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:15.279
are the best people to do it – the Belters’
new hope for an economic and political future

00:21:15.279 --> 00:21:20.869
is to become galactic shipping magnates . In
the book, Holden jokes that they should call

00:21:20.869 --> 00:21:26.269
the union “the spacing guild” – which
is a reference to a similar concept in Dune.

00:21:26.269 --> 00:21:31.489
So everyone agrees a Transport Union is a
good idea, but they can’t agree on who should

00:21:31.489 --> 00:21:33.340
be in charge of it.

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:38.749
After a century of conflict, the inner planets
and the Belters don’t trust each other.

00:21:38.749 --> 00:21:43.499
Avasarala suggests that Holden should be in
charge – because has worked with Earthers

00:21:43.499 --> 00:21:49.100
Martians and Belters fairly, he has experience
with the ring space and Medina Station, and

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:53.520
y’know, he’s the protagonist and he’s
very handsome, so of course he should be in

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:54.520
charge.

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:59.619
So Holden agrees to be the first President
of the Transport Union – the brave warrior

00:21:59.619 --> 00:22:04.229
protagonist becomes king in the end, like
Aragon in Lord of the Rings or the bloody

00:22:04.229 --> 00:22:05.759
Pevensie kids.

00:22:05.759 --> 00:22:11.690
But in an unexpected twist, Holden immediately
steps down and makes Drummer the new President

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:12.909
instead.

00:22:12.909 --> 00:22:19.499
He says if the Transport Union is the future
for the Belters, it should be led by a Belter

00:22:19.499 --> 00:22:22.450
. And Drummer is more qualified than Holden.

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:27.179
She has experience running Medina Station
in the ring space, and she was Medina’s

00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:29.350
captain back when it was the Behemoth.

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:34.220
Drummer did shipping and distribution work
bringing supplies to Ceres, which is exactly

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:39.740
what the Transport Union will do . Drummer
has proven her commitment to the Belt over

00:22:39.740 --> 00:22:44.539
and over, and she’s shown her willingness
to cooperate with Earth and Mars.

00:22:44.539 --> 00:22:50.519
Drummer was always the quintessential Belter,
and after six seasons of struggle, she brings

00:22:50.519 --> 00:22:52.190
hope for her people.

00:22:52.190 --> 00:22:58.120
It’s also a great character moment for Holden
to pull off this sneaky trick – he pretended

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:03.919
to agree to be President, under certain conditions
, plotting all along to give it to Drummer

00:23:03.919 --> 00:23:10.129
. Because Holden’s whole thing in the beginning
of the series was to be honest and open about

00:23:10.129 --> 00:23:11.129
everything.

00:23:11.129 --> 00:23:15.929
He thought he knew what was best for everyone,
he made the decisions, and he told everyone

00:23:15.929 --> 00:23:22.230
his true intentions . But this time, he hides
his true intentions, and gives the power to

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:23.510
someone else.

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:30.799
It shows how much Holden has changed and grown
from the naïve idealist he once was.

00:23:30.799 --> 00:23:36.239
Miller and Avasarala taught him that sometimes
it’s necessary to lie for the greater good

00:23:36.239 --> 00:23:41.470
. And Naomi and Drummer showed him that he
needs to share leadership with others . He

00:23:41.470 --> 00:23:45.710
is not personally responsible for running
the universe.

00:23:45.710 --> 00:23:52.860
Saving humanity is “a group project” .
Clarissa gives Amos a badge of a devil face.

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:57.220
Amos used to wear one like this, but apparently
lost it last season.

00:23:57.220 --> 00:24:02.909
Clarissa now replaces it, and makes one for
herself – as a super adorable symbol of

00:24:02.909 --> 00:24:03.909
their friendship.

00:24:03.909 --> 00:24:07.960
Though the badge has a dark backstory.

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:13.440
In the Expanse Origins comic book, we see
Amos and his friend Saru when they were sexually

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:15.549
exploited as children.

00:24:15.549 --> 00:24:23.119
Saru committed suicide, but he gave Amos his
devil badge, telling Amos to live and to “keep

00:24:23.119 --> 00:24:24.119
smiling”.

00:24:24.119 --> 00:24:30.659
So the devil badge represents Amos hiding
his trauma behind a mask, being emotionally

00:24:30.659 --> 00:24:32.759
detached to survive.

00:24:32.759 --> 00:24:40.259
But over six seasons, Amos grows and uses
his experience of trauma to help others – transforming

00:24:40.259 --> 00:24:45.009
a symbol of pain into one of connection and
hope.

00:24:45.009 --> 00:24:50.629
At the end of the finale, Holden says we still
don’t know what’s happening with the protomolecule,

00:24:50.629 --> 00:24:52.570
and Laconia and Duarte.

00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:57.399
At the end of the credits, we see the entities
still lurking in the ring.

00:24:57.399 --> 00:25:03.490
The Expanse TV show is ending without finishing
the story from the last three Expanse books.

00:25:03.490 --> 00:25:08.039
The creators of the Expanse say that they’re
just pausing the story, and that last three

00:25:08.039 --> 00:25:11.000
books might be adapted someday . It does make
sense to pause here, because Book 7 actually

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:12.000
starts 30 years after Book 6.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:18.099
Holden is eager to face this future, but Naomi
says let’s just stay and enjoy the moment

00:25:18.099 --> 00:25:23.299
in the present, as the Roci sails the vast
expanse.

00:25:23.299 --> 00:25:29.820
The Expanse is about aliens and spaceships
and explosions, and it’s really about the

00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:32.600
tragedy of human conflict.

00:25:32.600 --> 00:25:39.409
No matter how far we expand into the universe,
our politics and tribes divide us – heroes

00:25:39.409 --> 00:25:42.259
are those who try to unite us.

00:25:42.259 --> 00:25:45.809
At the end of the Expanse everything has changed.

00:25:45.809 --> 00:25:51.639
Humanity has expanded from just one solar
system to new worlds across a thousand stars.

00:25:51.639 --> 00:25:57.179
Earth is devastated, Mars is obsolete, the
Belt is transformed.

00:25:57.179 --> 00:26:02.840
But the old divisions remain – this isn’t
the end of war.

00:26:02.840 --> 00:26:09.030
So everything’s changed, but nothing’s
changed, really . At the end of Book 6, Anna

00:26:09.030 --> 00:26:12.789
and her family head for a new life on a new
world.

00:26:12.789 --> 00:26:18.480
She thinks no matter how far humanity expands,
we’re basically stuck with each other – we’re

00:26:18.480 --> 00:26:23.500
spending our lives together, and all we can
do is try to get along.

00:26:23.500 --> 00:26:29.979
If we’re gentle, maybe the stars will be
better off with us .

00:26:29.979 --> 00:26:34.909
Thanks for watching, and thanks to Amazon
Prime Video UK for sponsoring this video.

00:26:34.909 --> 00:26:39.440
